Program Name: Language
Number: \d*\.?\d+
String: ^"[\s\S]*"$
Identifier: ^[a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*$

Language is very similar to Lox in that it uses double quotations to mark strings,
numbers are handled the same way, and identifiers must start with a letter but can contain
numbers. It however does not require any special character to denote the end of a line
and strings can contain all white space types. It is also set up with common identifier tokens
such as: and, if, print, return, while, etc. While they do not do anything currently, the 
tokens are created.


There is no special set up for the scanner other than having access to the main python program
containing Language and a .language file. Entering it into the command line.

